docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:39:## 2. Coordination patterns that work
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:43:| Orchestrator–workers, isolated contexts | Anthropic research system: +90.2% vs single agent; tokens explain ~80% of variance; ~15× chat tokens; explicit effort-scaling rules (secondary summary) — https://theaiengineer.substack.com/p/how-anthropic-built-multi-agent-deep | Breadth, parallelisable work |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:44:| Verifier at the merge point | 180 configs, 3 families: independent agents amplify errors 17.2×, centralised 4.4×; centralised +80.8% on parallel tasks; **every** MAS −39–70% on sequential reasoning — https://research.google/blog/towards-a-science-of-scaling-agent-systems-when-and-why-agent-systems-work/ | Always, and pick topology by task shape |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:52:## 3. Known failure modes
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:55:2. **Context isolation → conflicting implicit decisions** — https://cognition.com/blog/dont-build-multi-agents
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:63:10. **Unvetted capability supply** — 10,000+ MCP servers, thin curation — https://www.truefoundry.com/blog/best-mcp-registries
