docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:1:# J1 — Round 1 judge (Claude)
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:6:## 1. Score table
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:20:- **C3:** horizontal, bossless, but no portfolio strategy owner; co-founder shrinks to a weekly packet · no taste capture or founder model · capability-gap recruitment: no unsupported mission type · emergent discovery + 30-min disputes; it flags its own overhead · fencing tokens, atomic leases, idempotency, effect gateway, partition rules: most engineered · read-and-outcome memory, replay, but no calibration per identity.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:22:- **C5:** lot compounds, Series runs businesses, but departments and T0–T3 are startup-shaped · raw-artifact Dailies Reel, circled takes, 19 min / 3 decisions · ladder fixes evidence not method, yet a fixed four-rung lifecycle nears a playbook · backlot reuse, self-greenlit T0–T1, second-unit swarms · tranches, single edit bay, completion guarantor; departments can bottleneck · mandatory strike makes N+1 cheaper; calibration charges missed upside.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:24:## 2. Strongest mechanism and most dangerous flaw
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:30:| C3 | **Fenced leases plus a scoped effect gateway.** Stale workers cannot act, and money and messages pass only through adapters that enforce margin floors and idempotency. | **No owner of direction.** The attention field optimises locally. Busywork is caught only after "two experiments without progress", and nobody holds the portfolio thesis between weekly packets. |
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:34:## 3. The best combination
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:38:already treats hybrids and Claude vs Codex as experimental arms. Its gaps are a runtime substrate, a continuous
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:43:| Evidence-linked world model, fenced leases, per-resource merge queue, effect gateway, idempotency, partition rules | **C3** | The Lab's coordination is thin. C3 is the most robust substrate, so it becomes the floor that the Lab runs on. |
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:69:## 4. What all five missed
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:73:3. **Counterparty agents:** customers, suppliers and competitors will send *their* agents — A2A commerce, negotiation, and defence against injection via tickets, reviews and inbound mail.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:75:5. **Model-release reflexes:** on each new model or tool, re-run the frozen benchmark for every config (C2's Fingerprint gate, generalised) *and* ask what it newly makes possible — capability jumps as strategy.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:81:## 5. Evidence checks against Round 0
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J1-judge-claude.md:85:- **C3 vs R0-A.** R0-A says a single strong agent beats any swarm on sequential reasoning and the target is an org that *chooses its shape per mission*; C3 makes swarm the default. Independent agents amplify errors 17.2× vs 4.4× centralised; per-resource merge queues only partly meet "every fan-out ends at a verifier". C3 cites no R0 source — honest as proposal, unevidenced as stigmergy.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:1:# R0 — Tiny teams with AI: what is actually achieved (Codex seat)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:7:## 1) Findings with sources
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:11:| **Base44 / Maor Shlomo** | A founder-owned AI app-building company achieved an acquisition with a tiny team. | June 2025: approximately **$80m announced initial consideration**, plus earn-outs; **eight employees**, so “solo” described ownership, not total labour. | [Wix announcement](https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2025/06/18/3101508/0/en/wix-further-expands-into-vibe-coding-with-acquisition-of-base44.html); [employee confirmation](https://techcrunch.com/2025/06/18/6-month-old-solo-owned-vibe-coder-base44-sells-to-wix-for-80m-cash/) | **High:** transaction; no proof the organisation ran autonomously. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:12:| **Cal AI** | AI consumer product with exceptional sales relative to its reported core payroll. | March 2026 acquisition announcement quotes **over $40m sales in the preceding 12 months**; acquisition reporting identifies **seven employees plus contractors**. | [Acquirer’s release](https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/03/02/3247439/0/en/myfitnesspal-acquires-cal-ai-expanding-on-its-position-as-the-leading-player-in-digital-nutrition-tracking.html); [staffing](https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/myfitnesspal-has-acquired-cal-ai-the-viral-calorie-app-built-by-teens/) | **High:** acquisition; **medium:** disclosed sales and staffing, unaudited here. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:29:## 2) Patterns — what the winners do
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:37:**Agent businesses combine persistent coordination with specialist tools.** The published interview with Eliason’s agent describes OpenClaw, file-based memory, Discord, AgentMail, Stripe, Supabase, Vercel, DigitalOcean, **Codex CLI and Claude Code**. Treat this as a reported architecture: an agent’s description of itself is not independent verification. [Interview](https://thenextnewthing.beehiiv.com/p/this-openclaw-earned-177-417)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:47:## 3) Failure modes observed
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:57:## 4) “What we should use”
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:68:8. **Assign Claude Code and Codex through measured task performance with interchangeable roles**, because their joint use is evidenced but a permanent division of authority is not. [Reported stack](https://thenextnewthing.beehiiv.com/p/this-openclaw-earned-177-417)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:77:## 5) Ideas nobody is doing yet that our organisation could
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:88:## 6) Where this hits the founder’s direction
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:90:The [founder’s direction](/Users/adamks/VibeCoding/agentvibe/.worktrees/ceo-2-1790613501/docs/vision-v3/00-FOUNDER-DIRECTION.md) asks for equal Claude Code/Codex workers, per-project autonomy, dynamic teams, organisational memory and a founder operating at the right altitude.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:1:# C5 — The Studio
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:5:## 1. The idea
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:9:## 2. System
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:17:  SETS[Sets: backlot of code, infra, brand kits, audiences] -->|leased| PROD
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:27:## 3. How work flows (no playbook)
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:29:1. **Coverage** (≤2 h, ≤$8). Three blind **readers**, drawn from both Claude and Codex, each return premise, comparables, failure modes and *pass/consider/recommend*. Disagreement is kept as signal.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:39:| T3 Release / Series pickup | ads, outbound, grade ≥ A2 | box office inside forecast band | per production |
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:43:## 4. The founder's seat — Studio Chief
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:50:## 5. Agents — cast, not hired
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:51:**Cast record:** `{title, expertise, skills[], tools[], model_family, sandbox, memory_scopes[], reel[], believability{domain→score}, rate}`. Agents carry titles only ("Growth Engineer"). The **reel** (past accepted takes) is what Casting reads. Launched only per call-sheet slot, as a Claude Code or Codex session.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:52:- **Claude and Codex are two equal talent pools.** For a new role, or when the two families are within 10% believability, both **screen-test** the same scene, blind-scored by Post. Winners are cast and losing takes are kept as data.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:54:- **Crew templates per tranche, learned:** T0 is 3 readers. T1 is a Director, 2 makers and 1 Post. T2 is a Director, a 1st AD, ≤5 makers per lane and 2 cross-family Post. Past 5 lanes the production splits into a second unit with its own AD. **Second-unit swarms** shoot 3–10 variants in parallel, and each swarm ends at a verifier.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:56:## 6. Coordination and non-interference
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:58:- **Stage booking = leases.** Sets (repos, databases, ad accounts, domains, audiences) are booked with expiring *read/shoot/strike* scopes. Two productions never hold *shoot* on the same set at once.
