docs/vision-system/research/L11-governance.md:17:**Design proposal:** an external-action authorization identifies legal principal, authenticated actor, capacity, represented entity, permitted activity, counterparty, amount, jurisdiction assumptions, expiry and delegation limits. Bind approval to the actual terms and payload; changed terms reopen it. Separate power to propose, execute, settle disputes and amend authority. Internal limits may not defeat a counterparty's legal claim: counsel must assess attribution and apparent authority. Preserve the distinction between an attempted transaction and confirmed acceptance.
