docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/technical-foundation-repairs-v1.md:11:The assumed surviving roots are the release/authorization service, its independent recovery storage and keys, controlled egress, and a separately reachable recovery administrator. Evidence claims additionally require their declared independent observation and interpretation roots. A compromised adapter may violate its native scope until provider containment succeeds; internal grants cannot constrain a stolen provider credential beyond actual provider enforcement. Admission must declare that exposure. Compromise of an issuer invalidates claims relying on its grants; compromise of release enforcement invalidates prevention claims; loss or compromise of every recovery root defeats trustworthy reconstruction. Malicious provider administrators, malicious ultimate company administrators, undisclosed off-platform promises, and host/kernel escapes beyond the tested isolation boundary remain exclusions. These actors or failures can bypass the available enforcement or observation roots; this design has no stronger surviving authority to promise protection. No claim survives every trust root failing together.
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/technical-foundation-repairs-v1.md:15:Research support is scoped. [L07](../../research/L07-security.md) supplies mediation and information-flow concerns; [L08](../../research/L08-reliability.md) distinguishes local transactions, external effects, fencing and recovery; [L12](../../research/L12-improvement.md) supplies evidence-path attacks. Primary product pages reopened for consequential uncertainties below were accessed on 2026-09-12. They describe vendor contracts, with vendor incentives; they do not validate this protocol. Recheck them before integration and on permission, version, retention, or semantic change, and no later than 2026-12-12. Every trace and falsifying test here is synthetic and unexecuted.
