docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/company-foundation-repairs-v1.md:17:The companion `technical-foundation-repairs-v1.md` owns release/consistency, independent effect durability, evidence dependencies, causal work limits, and invalidation enforcement. This document owns who decides, external standing, classification, and competent response. Its enforcement inputs are versioned `ResponsibilityAssignment`, `InteractionDetermination`, `ResponseDecision`, `GrievanceCase`, and `DeletionScope`. Their changes emit dependency changes; they do not directly rewrite external state. A denied or unavailable release returns to the duty custodian with its reason and remaining deadline. A newly discovered surviving promise must receive both a responsibility assignment and the companion’s recoverable obligation/effect linkage.
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/company-foundation-repairs-v1.md:60:States are `received → acknowledged → assessing → disposition-issued → remedy-pending → remedy-verified`, with independently visible `contested`, `escalated`, `awaiting-required-information`, and `unresolved`. Internal disposition is not counterparty agreement. A response names the responsible recipient, understandable issue and scope, evidence and limitations, reasons, proposed remedy or refusal, due dates, next progress update, and available independent escalation. Required information requests must explain relevance and preserve unaffected work; they cannot repeatedly reset the clock.
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/company-foundation-repairs-v1.md:68:Remedy authority names available correction, service completion, refund, access/deletion assistance, explanation, or other appropriately determined redress. Reserve costs and staff/service capacity against the actual principal and liabilities; caps describe what the delegate may release, not a unilateral cap on another person’s rights. Insufficient resources become a financing/continuity problem with an owned escalation, never a finding that nothing is owed. No new funding or engagement occurs from this proposal.
