docs/vision-system/planning/specification/04-human-operation.md:21:**SPECIFICATION.** Human records extend the common `RecordEnvelope` and exact `Ref`. The following fields are domain contracts to consolidate into the full schema track; they do not redefine release, identity or validity state.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/04-human-operation.md:36:**SPECIFICATION.** `CommittedPosition` is a presentation alias of the kernel's canonical `Position = {registry_generation:UInt64, sequence:UInt64, transaction_hash:Digest}`. Import inline `SourceWatermark = {source_id, source_revision, observed_at, complete_through?, omissions:string[]}` from the same contract. `Instant` and `generated_at` use canonical UTC timestamps with explicit `Z`. The source contract supplies expected interval and freshness limits; absent `complete_through` cannot imply complete enumeration. `operation_status_ref` is an exact reference to `OperationStatus`, carrying the authoritative operation, possible release, attempts, phase, effect knowledge, stop disposition, frontier and observations. Status is never an authority token. Projection position establishes what the view consumed, not universal world completeness or independently durable release. A generated summary includes selected/excluded original references and potentially lossy transformations. Hidden/private model reasoning is neither required nor claimed available; recorded explanation remains testimony with causal limits.
