docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/C-adaptive-coordination.md:11:[L13, countermodel D](../../research/L13-contrarian.md) supplies the coordination precedent: Smith’s [Contract Net Protocol](https://www.reidgsmith.com/The_Contract_Net_Protocol_Dec-1980.pdf), December 1980, describes announcements, bids, and awards; Erman et al.’s [Hearsay-II](https://mas.cs.umass.edu/Documents/Erman_Hearsay80.pdf), June 1980, coordinates knowledge sources through shared hypotheses. Its §4.3 also reports poor results when specialized internal activity was forced into the general blackboard. These primary system reports motivate limited shared coordination, not a claim of business effectiveness. Both were reopened on 2026-09-12; no experiment was reproduced.
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/C-adaptive-coordination.md:17:The shared blackboard is a permission-filtered collection of records and references, not everybody’s conversation history. Six record families suffice; the directive’s schema subjects remain distinguishable types or relations within them, rather than becoming 46 services.
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/C-adaptive-coordination.md:23:| Obligations and resources | Principal, counterparty, promised performance, applicable duty, deadline, discharge authority, cash, allowance, execution slots, attention and reserves. Proposed → active → performed, disputed, discharged, transferred, or surviving | A named accountable steward owns continuity; accounting/provider sources own their native facts. Only authorized evidence rules permit discharge |
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/10-components-authority-traceability.md:25:**SPECIFICATION.** Failure behavior follows the affected dependency and consequence. Missing required identity, witness, trusted time, disclosure lineage or exact accepted predicate denies dependent authority. D0 ephemeral work, genuinely saved D1 local staging/export and D2 witnessed transitions have different claims. Already admitted local work may continue within surviving context, lease and allowance. An offline browser draft is neither a server StageRef nor independently durable; a primary-ahead command row is not a witnessed acceptance. Actual owed service still needs an accepted competent route or a truthful missed-duty account. A system that only refuses safely has not demonstrated useful company operation.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/10-components-authority-traceability.md:40:| Launch requirements | An independently admitted requirements manifest predates readiness assembly. Every unique requirement ID joins exactly one binding of exact subject/version, predicate and current accepted EvidenceJudgment. No omissions, duplicates, substitution across distinct subjects or readiness self-evidence. A changed requirement, child or mapping invalidates dependent readiness before release. |
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/10-components-authority-traceability.md:45:| Stop and retry | Request, future-release fence, worker cessation, external reconciliation and remedy completion are separate. G bounds a kernel buffer at the named hook; later wire frames/provider effects and partial requests remain possible. Unknown effects retain holds and cannot receive an automatic fresh mutation merely because an acknowledgement was lost. |
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md:13:**SPECIFICATION.** Every procedure runs as an admitted `WorkOrder` through S1-C02. Its inputs are exact catalog ports plus loader-controlled context, causal allowance, lease and acceptance owner. It returns staged artifact references, attributable attempt reports, observations, checkpoint and unfinished duties through S1-C03. All commands use the kernel’s `POST /v1/commands`, including `command_id`, version, company/principal, expected revisions, causal episode and authority references. Transport supplies authenticated actor identity. Kernel `accepted` means the transition is committed and independently witnessed; it does not mean an outward effect occurred or a customer was satisfied. `durability_pending` requires lookup with the same command ID; a primary row cannot supply the missing witness.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md:27:**SPECIFICATION.** S1-C04 owns grants, reservations, release, conflict identity and resource bounds; C05 owns validity/lineage; C06 owns evidence/acceptance; C07 owns human/external responsibility; C08 owns independent recovery; C09 presents projections. `01-contract-kernel.md` and `02-authority-recovery.md` are companion specification contracts authored separately. This file neither assigns production credentials to a capability nor duplicates their grant/release state machines.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md:49:**SPECIFICATION.** Mapping changes that reveal overlapping entitlements or new required participants follow technical R1: fence combined scope, preserve old unknown holds, invalidate obsolete unreleased preparations, reconcile new identities and establish a common release order before resuming. A projection-only rename cannot move a customer promise, money or rights into a different principal.
docs/vision-system/planning/reviews/D-technical.md:35:**Falsifying test:** Lose every primary record after the backup while allowing one external effect to occur. Restore with intact revocation/deletion state but incomplete provider history. Any second effect, released exposure, or assertion that no uncertainty exists falsifies the recovery claim.
docs/vision-system/planning/reviews/D-technical.md:49:**Required foundational decision:** Choose an explicit release/commit protocol and revocation cutoff: who can durably authorize the complete bundle, what each issuer promises after preparation, and what happens during partitions, expiry, or coordinator loss. A narrow cross-issuer coordinator need not become a company planner, but its existence, availability cost, and recovery authority must be acknowledged.
docs/vision-system/planning/reviews/D-technical.md:215:| Foundational coherence | **Conditional:** recovery and semantic enforcement need closure. | **Conditional:** cross-issuer release/revocation is a foundational fork. | **Conditional:** useful progress under sustained disturbance is unresolved. |
