docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/AC-foundational-distinction.md:30:| **Retire** | The charter's authorized assessor may certify evidence-supported resolution, duplication into an acknowledged surviving inquiry, exhausted investigation with explicit unresolved disposition, or an authorized withdrawal. | A production planner cannot close the question by closing its work order. Any underlying obligation survives unless its actual discharge authority permits release. |
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/AC-foundational-distinction.md:69:The simpler competitor gives A full event-driven adaptation, ordinary reserved maintenance capacity, a scheduled cross-function review, temporary investigators, and explicit unresolved-case records. It lacks only the compulsory independent inquiry jurisdiction being tested. A second control implements the same charter rights through a case engine. If that second control is equivalent, the result refutes blackboard-specific necessity; it does not make CMMN inflexible. If scheduled review delivers equivalent useful discovery, omissions and continuity at lower full cost, reject the additional C2 rights as the organizing choice.
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/AC-foundational-distinction.md:88:The eight common scenarios remain required, with these additional checks: **(1)** launch must not retire contradictory research; **(2)** a claim inquiry cannot override opt-out or send restrictions; **(3)** invoice inquiry cannot fabricate reconciliation or filing; **(4)** inquiry resumption cannot release an unknown refund hold; **(5)** two ventures cannot appropriate the same inquiry or service reserve; **(6)** changed intent can revoke future inquiry grants but preserves reasons and surviving duties; **(7)** poisoning cannot create standing or let an improver change its assessor; **(8)** restoration cannot resurrect a charter, and closure needs accepted inquiry dispositions alongside actual external obligations. Original C §8 supplies the full scenarios and falsifiers; all remain unexecuted.
docs/vision-system/planning/F2/00-acceptance-protocol.md:15:**Fixed unless a lane returns a specific falsifier**, per [HANDOFF §0.5](../HANDOFF-F2-agents-work-layer.md): the consequence and release boundary; evidence and acceptance; recovery; human responsibility; the founder-competence mechanism; whole-company scope. A candidate may reopen any of these **only** with a named counterexample routed to the founder as a decision packet ([DIRECTIVE §3](../../inputs/DIRECTIVE.md)), never by preference and never silently. A candidate that quietly relaxes a fixed boundary fails dimension W2 whatever else it achieves.
docs/vision-system/planning/F2/00-acceptance-protocol.md:34:| **W2** | **Coherence with the fixed boundaries** | Hand the candidate and [`01-contract-kernel.md`](../specification/01-contract-kernel.md), [`02-authority-recovery.md`](../specification/02-authority-recovery.md) and [`06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md`](../specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md) to two implementers. Ask each what "accepted" means and who may release an external effect. | Compatible answers. Fails if a local "done" in the work layer discharges an obligation, accepts an outcome, or releases an effect that [`02-architecture-selection.md` §3](../02-architecture-selection.md) assigns elsewhere — and fails harder if the candidate changed a fixed boundary without a decision packet. |
docs/vision-system/planning/F2/00-acceptance-protocol.md:36:| **W4** | **Cost and capacity under subscription** | Price the candidate's normal week against its own comparators under roughly $200/month Claude Code plus $200/month Codex, with reset windows and a concurrency limit. Then make a lane hit a weekly cap mid-attempt. | Both **money spent and scarce capacity consumed**, separately ([DIRECTIVE §8.21](../../inputs/DIRECTIVE.md)); queued work and explicit fallback policy. Fails on any **silent fallback to a metered API**, on a token count offered as a capacity model, or on a design whose cost is only defensible at per-token prices. |
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/A-records-and-cases.md:9:The organizing objects are a company’s directions, business records, and open cases. A case holds an outcome needing attention, rather than representing an artificial employee. It may concern an opportunity, product release, customer dispute, filing, incident, or closure. Stable procedures are attached to cases where helpful; unfamiliar work can acquire new steps without pretending its path was known beforehand.
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/A-records-and-cases.md:19:| Procedures and changes | Versioned instructions, skills, tool contracts, workflows, configurations, evaluations, defects, experiments, releases, and rollback arrangements. |
docs/vision-system/planning/candidates/A-records-and-cases.md:23:The core owns accepted company intent, case state, authority, reservations, and recorded obligations. Domain systems retain authoritative native records: accounting entries belong to accounting; payment settlement is established through the provider or bank; a counterparty’s disputed acceptance is not overwritten by an internal status. Each integration states which fields it owns and which are cached observations. [L02, operations](../../research/L02-operations.md); [L13, countermodel A](../../research/L13-contrarian.md).
