":"criterion","findings":["RC-01"],"decisions":[],"why":"RC-01 removed `not(native_correlated delivered)` from this criterion because it contradicted the only edge that could reach the phase. A conjunct removed for a stated reason is one removal away from the next one having no reason at all, so what REMAINS is pinned: the failure is owned, not merely declared.","require":[{"op":"nonempty_fields","field_paths_include":["/payload/remaining_duties","/payload/receipts","/payload/service_window"],"why":"the obligations survive on the record, and the receipts actually obtained and the window are recorded -- a failure that recorded none of these would be a closure wearing the word failure"},{"op":"related_phases","bindings":[{"field_path":"/payload/performer_assignment","states_exactly":["accepted"],"optional":false}],"why":"CAP-30: failure creates a support/remedy duty, and a duty with no accepted performer is unowned"}]},{"predicate_id":"criterion.GrievanceCase.remedy_authorized.v1","kind":"criterion","findings":["G4-02"],"decisions":[],"why":"G4-02: `remedy_reservation_refs` was required in the payload and used by 0 predicates, and this criterion carried `nonempty_fields: []` -- so a remedy could be authorized with no reservation at all, which is what made CAP-42's funded remedy prose.","require":[{"op":"nonempty_fields","field_paths_include":["/payload/remedy_reservation_refs"],"why":"an empty reservation list is the exact shape the finding names"},{"op":"related_phases","bindings":[{"field_path":"/payload/remedy_reservation_refs","states_exactly":["held","partly_consumed"],"optional":false}],"why":"the funding is ACTUALLY RESERVED: every entry resolves to a live Reservation. A released or expired reservation funds nothing."}]},{"predicate_id":"criterion.GrievanceCase.triaged.v1","kind":"criterion","findings":["G4-01"],"decisions":[],"why":"G4-01: `disputed_custodian` is required on GrievanceCase and was read by 0 of 2,255 predicates. The criterion carries the two refs the guard's `neq` compares; erase them here and the comparison one layer up compares absent fields.","require":[{"op":"nonempty_fields","field_paths_include":["/payload/custodian_assignment_ref","/payload/independent_escalation_assignment_ref"],"why":"both sides of the conflict-of-interest comparison must be recorded at triage"},{"op":"related_phases","bindings":[{"field_path":"/payload/custodian_assignment_ref","states_exactly":["accepted"],"optional":false}],"why":"the custodian has accepted the case"}]},{"predicate_id":"criterion.SalesAgreement.performed.v1","kind":"criterion","findings":["G2-01","RC-02"],"decisions":["AD-013"],"why":"The original (d): `performed` demanded byte-identical field_paths to `accepted`, the agreement had no relation to a Fulfillment, and the only native object reachable was the payment -- so a buyer could pay, the Fulfillment stay `proposed`, every Obligation stay `recognized`, and the sale reach `performed` with nothing objecting. AD-013 decides it: delivery, not payment. These three rows ARE that decision, and the recheck's one-hunk weakening removed all three at once.","require":[{"op":"nonempty_fields","field_paths_include":["/payload/fulfillment_ref","/payload/obligation_refs"],"why":"the agreement must NAME its own Fulfillment and its obligations; without these two paths the phases below bind to nothing"},{"op":"related_phases","bindings":[{"field_path":"/payload/fulfillment_ref","states_exactly":["delivered"],"optional":false},{"field_path":"/payload/obligation_refs","states_exactly":["discharged","transferred"],"optional":false}],"why":"AD-013: that Fulfillment is currently `delivered` and every linked Obligation is `discharged` or `transferred`. `optional: true` on either would readmit the counterexample with the field simply absent."},{"op":"native_correlated","result":"delivered","why":"AD-013: the correlated native object is the DELIVERY. `result: \"performed\"` is what it said before the repair and correlates the sale to