docs/vision-system/planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md:13:**SPECIFICATION.** All records use canonical `RecordEnvelope`, exact `Ref`, UTC timestamps, `Position`, resource quantities and kernel command results. `accepted` requires a committed, independently witnessed transition. It is distinct from output acceptance, effect observation, customer acceptance and duty discharge. Witness outage permits only existing admitted local computation within its surviving lease/context/allowance and the kernel's explicitly local `StageRef` save/export route. A StageRef is not a Ref, and importing it revalidates current restrictions. This document does not create another durability or receipt protocol.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md:23:**SPECIFICATION.** **An executor's grant scope is a proposal right; C04 performs every release** (R-X01, closing AT-M1-04). An executor may narrow what it asks for and may never widen what it holds, and the ability to propose a scope is never the ability to release under it. This is the only statement of that rule in this chapter; §11's release column is where it binds.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md:53:**The release authorisation is NOT sampled, per effect.** An outward release at the economic/contractual class requires a human approver for that effect (§7, R-G11). Sampling a release means releasing the unsampled ones with no approver, which is not a lighter version of the rule but its absence. **This half is unsampleable by construction, and that is the explicit statement the second limb asked for.**
