docs/vision-system/planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md:102:**SPECIFICATION.** `EvaluationPlan` is registered before seeing treatment results: subject/version, requirement/claim, unit/population, intended use, outcome and process criteria, forbidden outcomes, comparison, selection/assignment, resources, evaluator/labels, independence roots, trial/reset rules, stopping/analysis and reopening. `EvaluationRun` records every selected unit and attempt, including noncompletion, raw observations, cost/latency and protocol deviations. `Review` links a competent reviewer's attributable findings and limitations. Canonical EvidenceJudgment owns accepted scope; EvaluationRun or Review has no independent release authority. Its proposed state is unfinished assessment; inconclusive is a completed assessment that cannot establish its subject predicate; rejected is an adverse judgment; contested means disputed evidence, not automatic rejection. Later reassessment creates a witnessed revision with historical reasons retained. Acceptance of an uncertainty report establishes only that exact report criterion. Product, launch, capacity and effect gates require their exact current accepted subject/version/predicate bindings and complete evidence closure.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md:157:**SPECIFICATION.** Retain S0 with native tools, competent manual release and comparable external obligations, resources, recovery and owner allowance. Preserve G's four EAS-R1 tests separately: each design's own rights; business effectiveness at matched external obligations/resources/information/service; case versus shared-hypothesis representation with identical C2 rights; and fully adaptive A/S1 with protected discovery plus scheduled cross-domain review but no compulsory independent inquiry jurisdiction. Do not force equal internal deadlines that erase the treatment or score lawful S1 deferral as violation of C2's rule. No ontology, blackboard or agent count receives credit by existing.
