docs/vision-system/planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md:13:**SPECIFICATION.** The operational profile is specified in authority/recovery section 2. PostgreSQL has one admitted writer per registry generation, an independently administered synchronous recovery standby, and a recovery witness reading that standby. The witness's separate small writable PostgreSQL cluster holds receipt/frontier state; it is not another departmental authority. There is no automatic failover, asynchronous release mode, or quorum election implemented by application workers.
